{#-
  Cisco IOS / IOS-XE -- local accounts.

  Negations come first, in the same config push as the rewrite: an account
  whose hash type is changing (a legacy `password 7`) will not accept a new
  `secret` on top, so it has to be removed and written back.

  Available variables:
    remove     list[Entry]  accounts to negate; entry.line is `username <name>`
    add        list[str]    accounts to write
    users      {name: password}  plaintext, or a hash when hash_type is set
    privilege  str|None
    role       str|None     EOS only; unused here
    algorithm  str|None     md5 | sha256 | scrypt -- IOS `algorithm-type`
    hash_type  str|None     5 | 8 | 9 -- the value is already hashed
-#}
{% for entry in remove %}
no {{ entry.line }}
{% endfor %}
{% for name in add %}
username {{ name }}{% if privilege %} privilege {{ privilege }}{% endif %}{% if hash_type %} secret {{ hash_type }} {{ users[name] }}{% elif algorithm %} algorithm-type {{ algorithm }} secret {{ users[name] }}{% else %} secret {{ users[name] }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
